00:04:24,444 --> 00:04:30,444
First Contact. Last Stand.

2
00:08:48,888 --> 00:08:54,888
Cowboys & Aliens is a action, science fiction,
thriller film directed by Jon Favreau.

3
00:13:13,333 --> 00:13:19,333
A stranger stumbles into the desert town of Absolution with no memory
of his past and a futuristic shackle around his wrist.

4
00:17:37,777 --> 00:17:43,777
With the help of mysterious beauty Ella and the iron-fisted Colonel Dolarhyde, he finds himself leading an unlikely posse of
cowboys, outlaws, and Apache warriors against a common enemy from beyond this world in an epic showdown for survival.

5
00:22:02,222 --> 00:22:08,222
Jake Lonergan, played by Daniel Craig.

6
00:26:26,666 --> 00:26:32,666
Woodrow Dolarhyde, played by Harrison Ford.

7
00:30:51,111 --> 00:30:57,111
Ella Swenson, played by Olivia Wilde.

8
00:35:15,555 --> 00:35:21,555
Doc, played by Sam Rockwell.

9
00:39:40,000 --> 00:39:46,000
Nat Colorado, played by Adam Beach.

10
00:44:04,444 --> 00:44:10,444
Percy Dolarhyde, played by Paul Dano.

11
00:48:28,888 --> 00:48:34,888
Cowboys & Aliens is a 2011 space Western action thriller film directed by Jon Favreau and starring Daniel
Craig, Harrison Ford, Olivia Wilde, Sam Rockwell, Adam Beach, Paul Dano, and Noah Ringer.

12
00:52:53,333 --> 00:52:59,333
The film is based on the 2006 Platinum Studios graphic novel of
the same name created by Scott Mitchell Rosenberg.

13
00:57:17,777 --> 00:57:23,777
Set in the Southwestern United States in a retro-futuristic version of the 1870s, the film follows an amnesiac outlaw (Craig), a wealthy powerful
cattleman (Ford) and a mysterious woman (Wilde) who must ally to save a group of townspeople who have been abducted by aliens.

14
01:01:42,222 --> 01:01:48,222
The screenplay was written by Roberto Orci, Alex Kurtzman, Damon Lindelof, Mark Fergus and
Hawk Ostby, based on a screen story by the latter two along with Steve Oedekerk.

15
01:06:06,666 --> 01:06:12,666
The film was produced by Brian Grazer, Ron Howard, Kurtzman, Orci, and Rosenberg,
with Steven Spielberg and Favreau serving as executive producers.

16
01:10:31,111 --> 01:10:37,111
The project began development in April 1997, when Universal Pictures and DreamWorks Pictures bought film
rights to a concept pitched by Rosenberg which he described as a graphic novel in development.

17
01:14:55,555 --> 01:15:01,555
After the graphic novel was published in 2006, development on the film was
begun again, and Favreau signed on as director in September 2009.

18
01:19:20,000 --> 01:19:26,000
On a budget of $163 million, filming for Cowboys & Aliens
began in June 2010, in New Mexico and California.

19
01:23:44,444 --> 01:23:50,444
Despite studio pressure to release the film in 3-D, Favreau chose to film traditionally and in
anamorphic format (widescreen picture on standard 35 mm film) to further a "classic movie feel".

20
01:28:08,888 --> 01:28:14,888
Measures were taken to maintain a serious Western element despite
the film's "inherently comic" title and premise.

21
01:32:33,333 --> 01:32:39,333
The film's aliens were designed to be "cool and captivating", with some details, such as a fungus that grows on
their wounds, created to depict the creatures as frontiersmen facing adversity in an unfamiliar place.

22
01:36:57,777 --> 01:37:03,777
Cowboys & Aliens premiered at the 2011 San Diego Comic-Con and was released
theatrically in the United States by Universal Pictures on July 29.

23
01:41:22,222 --> 01:41:28,222
The film underperformed at the box office, earning
$174.8 million on a $163 million budget.

24
01:45:46,666 --> 01:45:52,666
Cowboys & Aliens received mixed reviews, with critics generally praising its
acting and special effects, but criticizing the screenplay and tone.

25
01:50:11,111 --> 01:50:17,111
The film explores themes of spacecraft, sheriff, robbery, escape, arizona.

26
01:54:35,555 --> 01:54:41,555
The tone is thought_provoking and intense.
